  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient is a 74\u2011year\u2011old woman with a long history of type 2 diabetes diagnosed in 1995, complicated by progressive diabetic nephropathy. Kidney disease progressed from stage 1 in 2007 to stage 4 by 2015, and she is currently awaiting renal transplantation. She suffered an acute STEMI in 2010 and has chronic coronary disease, aortic valve stenosis and a prior aortic valve replacement (2005). Hypertriglyceridemia and metabolic syndrome have been present since the mid\u20111990s. Diabetic neuropathy, proteinuria, and micro\u2011albuminuria indicate ongoing microvascular damage. Psychosocial stressors (stress, intimate\u2011partner abuse, low education, unemployment, criminal record) have been documented since 2015\u20112018. The medication list is limited to mixed\u2011insulin therapy and low\u2011dose aspirin, with no antihypertensives, statin, ACE\u2011I/ARB, or other CKD\u2011directed agents. The most recent laboratory data (A1c 3.9\u202f%) are from 2018, and no recent vital signs or renal function values are available.",
